## 🧬 **MOLECULAR DOCKING & DRUG DESIGN**

### 1. **AutoDock Vina**
**What it does:** Molecular docking to predict how small molecules bind to proteins
- **Use Case:** Test if your drug candidate fits into disease protein targets
- **Learning Curve:** 2-3 weeks
- **Real Application:** Screen 10,000 compounds against COVID-19 protease
- **Download:** [http://vina.scripps.edu](http://vina.scripps.edu)
- **Tutorial Time:** 20 hours to master

### 2. **PyMOL (Open Source)**
**What it does:** 3D visualization of proteins and drug interactions
- **Use Case:** See exactly how drugs fit in protein pockets
- **Learning Curve:** 1 week for basics
- **Real Application:** Visualize antibody-antigen interactions
- **Download:** [https://pymol.org/2/](https://pymol.org/2/)
- **Cool Feature:** Make publication-quality molecular movies

### 3. **SwissDock**
**What it does:** Web-based molecular docking without installation
- **Use Case:** Quick drug-protein binding predictions
- **Learning Curve:** 2-3 days
- **Real Application:** Design better versions of existing drugs
- **Access:** [http://www.swissdock.ch](http://www.swissdock.ch)
- **Advantage:** No coding required

### 4. **UCSF Chimera**
**What it does:** Molecular modeling and drug design visualization
- **Use Case:** Analyze protein structures and design drugs
- **Learning Curve:** 2 weeks
- **Real Application:** Find druggable pockets in proteins
- **Download:** [https://www.cgl.ucsf.edu/chimera/](https://www.cgl.ucsf.edu/chimera/)
- **Special:** Great for beginners

### 5. **Open Babel**
**What it does:** Convert between 100+ molecular file formats
- **Use Case:** Prepare molecules for different software
- **Learning Curve:** 3-4 days
- **Real Application:** Build molecular databases
- **Download:** [http://openbabel.org](http://openbabel.org)
- **Power:** Command-line automation for thousands of molecules

