## 🧪 **BIOINFORMATICS & GENOMICS**

### 1. **BLAST (NCBI)**
**What it does:** Find similar DNA/protein sequences
- **Use Case:** Identify unknown genes, find drug targets
- **Learning Curve:** 1 day basics, 2 weeks advanced
- **Real Application:** Discover new antibiotics from bacteria
- **Access:** [https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)
- **Speed:** Search billions of sequences in seconds

### 2. **Galaxy Platform**
**What it does:** Web-based platform for genomic analysis
- **Use Case:** Analyze DNA sequencing data without coding
- **Learning Curve:** 1 week
- **Real Application:** Find disease-causing mutations
- **Access:** [https://usegalaxy.org](https://usegalaxy.org)
- **Tools:** 8000+ bioinformatics tools

### 3. **Bioconductor (R)**
**What it does:** Genomic data analysis in R
- **Use Case:** Analyze gene expression, find drug targets
- **Learning Curve:** 1 month (R knowledge helpful)
- **Real Application:** Identify cancer biomarkers
- **Install:** Within R: `BiocManager::install()`
- **Packages:** 2000+ specialized tools

### 4. **MEGA (Molecular Evolutionary Genetics Analysis)**
**What it does:** Evolutionary analysis of DNA and proteins
- **Use Case:** Track virus mutations, predict resistance
- **Learning Curve:** 1-2 weeks
- **Real Application:** Design universal vaccines
- **Download:** [https://www.megasoftware.net](https://www.megasoftware.net)
- **Feature:** Beautiful phylogenetic trees

### 5. **Cytoscape**
**What it does:** Network analysis and visualization
- **Use Case:** Map drug-protein interaction networks
- **Learning Curve:** 2 weeks
- **Real Application:** Find new drug combinations
- **Download:** [https://cytoscape.org](https://cytoscape.org)
- **Apps:** 350+ plugins for specialized analysis

